1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,350
We often try to save money for a variety of different reasons.
我们总会出于各种各样的原因存钱。

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:13,000
It might be to save up for a new computer, put money aside into a rainy-day fund or put a deposit down for a mortgage on a house.
可能是为了攒钱买一台新电脑，为应急基金预留一笔钱，或是为买房的按揭贷款支付首付。

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:23,470
Learning how to save is important, but a recent study showed that over half of all 22 – 29-year-olds living in the UK have no savings at all.
学会存钱至关重要，但最近一项研究显示，在英国22至29岁的人群中，超过半数的人根本没有存款。

4
00:00:23,470 --> 00:00:28,770
Did they splurge and splash out on too many things, or are there other factors?
是他们挥霍无度、花钱大手大脚，还是另有原因？

5
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:31,700
And how can we become better savers?
我们又该如何成为更会存钱的人呢？

6
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:40,790
Many young people in the UK choose to live away from home, and the cost of renting can impact the amount we can tuck away in our savings.
许多英国年轻人选择离家独居，高昂的房租会直接影响我们能存下的钱数。

7
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:54,550
On top of that, according to a 2017 study, there is a huge pay gap in people in their twenties in the UK, with the top 10% earning 4.3 times per week as the lowest earners.
此外，2017年的一项研究表明，英国二十多岁年轻人的收入差距悬殊，收入最高的10%人群周薪是收入最低人群的4.3倍。

8
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:59,450
Possibly the mentality of ‘saving more when I earn more’ has crept in.
或许正是“等赚得多了再多存钱”的心态在悄然作祟。

9
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:11,260
However, there were some positives, with the number of people in debt, not including student loans for university, having fallen from 49% 10 years ago to 37%.
不过也有一些积极的趋势：不含大学助学贷款在内的负债人群比例，已从十年前的49%降至如今的37%。

10
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:14,750
So, how can we improve our ability to save?
那么，我们该如何提升存钱能力呢？

11
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:18,260
First off, put a stop to those impulse buys.
首先，杜绝冲动消费。

12
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:24,610
Ask yourself if you really need to buy something, even if it is on sale or looks like a bargain.
就算商品正在打折，或是看起来很划算，也要先问问自己是否真的需要。

13
00:01:24,610 --> 00:01:30,580
One way you could control your spending urges is by using cash rather than card.
控制消费欲望的一个办法是使用现金而非银行卡支付。

14
00:01:30,580 --> 00:01:37,210
Withdrawing cash before you go to a restaurant or shopping sets a fixed budget you must adhere to.
去餐厅吃饭或购物前先取好现金，这样就能设定一个必须遵守的固定预算。

15
00:01:37,210 --> 00:01:45,490
Also, any change that comes from your transactions when you’re using cash can be put in jar and deposited into your account.
此外，用现金交易时收到的零钱可以放进存钱罐，之后再存入银行账户。

16
00:01:45,490 --> 00:01:57,420
Finally, setting up a standing order from your current account into your savings just after you receive your salary will ensure you have some money set aside for a time that you might need it.
最后，在发薪后立即设置自动转账，把钱从活期账户转入储蓄账户，这样就能确保为不时之需存下一笔钱。

17
00:01:57,420 --> 00:02:03,830
Just after getting paid is a good idea for this as it means you save before you’ve had the chance to spend.
发薪之后马上就转是一个好主意，因为这意味着你还没有花钱的机会，钱就已经被存起来了。

18
00:02:03,830 --> 00:02:12,640
While there is some good news about debt for the twenty-somethings in the UK, the fact that over half have no savings is seen as a cause for concern.
尽管英国二十多岁人群的负债情况有了些许好转，但半数以上的人毫无存款这一事实，依然引发了人们的担忧。

19
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:18,160
While it could be due to some economic disparity, there may be some other factors at play.
这或许是经济差距造成的，但也可能涉及其他因素。

20
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:22,920
However, there are some actions we can take to help us all become better savers.
不过，我们确实可以采取一些措施，让自己变得更擅长储蓄。
